# Place the following BizHawk 2.11.2 reference assemblies here:
#   BizHawk.Client.Common.dll
#   BizHawk.Common.dll
#   BizHawk.Emulation.Common.dll
#   EmuHawk.exe
#
# They must come from the ppicinic/BizHawk fork, branch fix/4535-sticky-analog, which
# carries the fix for TASEmulators/BizHawk#4535 (sticky analog XOR-cancelled to neutral
# by mouse-bound axes -- this broke NDS touch input via joypad.setanalog).
#
# Build that fork and copy from its output/ directory:
#   <fork>\output\dll\BizHawk.Client.Common.dll
#   <fork>\output\dll\BizHawk.Common.dll
#   <fork>\output\dll\BizHawk.Emulation.Common.dll
#   <fork>\output\EmuHawk.exe
#
# Build the fork with Dist/BuildRelease.sh (not a bare `dotnet build`) so the assemblies
# are stamped 2.11.2.0. A bare build stamps them 1.0.0.0, and BotServer.dll then fails to
# bind against the real EmuHawk process at runtime.
#
# These files are gitignored (binary DLLs should not be committed).
